meta {
	name: 04_TwoDifferentPackagesAtOnce
	seq: 4
}

docs {
	Scenario: The requester asks for two different packages at once

		Given the approver has no pending request from the requester for either package
		When the requester asks for both packages at the same time
		Then both calls return 200, with one request each
		And the requester has exactly one pending request per package
		Finally the requester withdraws the pending requests to clean up

	Both calls queue the same pending notification to the approver, so one of them collides
	on the outbox and has to retry (`SaveChangesWithOutboxRetry`, #3937). A 500 here means that
	retry is broken. This already works today, so the scenario runs in every enabled environment.
}
